#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379166 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72fd3cc6-fee5-5249-b60d-a672a32adb6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379168} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3626d4-1d1f-5ad1-b0b5-e62fc52f4b1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379169} {:answer/id #uuid "ccdb75c0-2295-5bbe-ae11-f0cae2afd0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379170} {:answer/id #uuid "7760b649-f606-5f12-a086-ad38f1b32a12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379171} {:answer/id #uuid "91e137ae-fe57-51ad-a368-cca4f25f01ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccdb75c0-2295-5bbe-ae11-f0cae2afd0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379170} :answer-field/id #uuid "903b870b-9442-58e1-a837-1bde2f59340b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c5aa2130-3437-5b23-b921-671ec9c0b0ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-110974" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -2 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k-2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 0=k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-10,$ which means that $k=10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36ac12c1-8d23-5be7-a255-7bbcd4eef46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379175} {:answer/id #uuid "4de2621f-abbe-5d3f-8ab2-99537a0698b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379176} {:answer/id #uuid "88017c7b-5ba6-525f-a80d-2305a1af72d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379177} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1272a1-d8f1-544b-8d52-c8f2082b0917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379178} {:answer/id #uuid "9d0c72e9-d579-5d4b-abb6-e2352506a3af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36ac12c1-8d23-5be7-a255-7bbcd4eef46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379175} :answer-field/id #uuid "8979069e-acc9-5e1e-bbb9-4e01bc953da7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a7d73384-0a7c-5be0-8c8c-14e2cdf3bb45" :question/math-academy-id "q-111050" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -15 & 0 & 20 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 7 & -1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{4}=-2 \\\\ 0=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=2.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120442 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e50345c-dafb-5606-bf2f-0b5b61965f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379181} {:answer/id #uuid "d585bf2a-23cd-5d90-ad7c-01aac06079e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379182} {:answer/id #uuid "1ed888f5-9a42-576a-9439-909c12a2aa42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379183} {:answer/id #uuid "255885b8-92e4-526e-8a76-1e0ebcc8d39b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379184} {:answer/id #uuid "3f59f455-b01b-5da8-87da-67e459f12a72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e50345c-dafb-5606-bf2f-0b5b61965f4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(E)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379181} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bc53ac7-23c7-5f40-8afa-edec101621be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0554a363-6902-58e6-8a93-41a3bab0a0ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-74080" :question/problem "The matrix $E$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(E).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}\\cdot {x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{e}_{1}+{x}_{2}{e}_{2}+{x}_{3}{e}_{3}+{x}_{4}{e}_{4},$ and ${e}_{1}$, ${e}_{2}$, ${e}_{3}$, and ${e}_{4}$ are respective columns of $E.$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379186 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a557ee8d-51a9-5387-a28c-67ffefed55b4" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Value of an Unknown Given a Vector That’s in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2174c897-5862-5221-8787-7bc085ca705c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379188} {:answer/id #uuid "551f6eba-0d08-55bf-b62a-1f370731a475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379189} {:answer/id #uuid "82fea190-b04d-5c74-bd5d-4d54deffa25c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379190} {:answer/id #uuid "d885c88c-f693-572e-ad9a-e0f689ad96d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379191} {:answer/id #uuid "2260775e-fc56-553a-958b-5a9b2e0f8545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82fea190-b04d-5c74-bd5d-4d54deffa25c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379190} :answer-field/id #uuid "febcff31-456f-5038-9642-c05427f99f40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ad6fcbc-db24-5596-8c00-5b434344d5b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-74212" :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $L=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k-11 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & k-11 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1 & k-11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ 0=k-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-16,$ which means that $k=16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "87dc8398-fb5c-564b-a796-db15ff30d72c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector Is in the Column Space of a Larger Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6249785-9289-5c5e-b1b7-6a64649145e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379195} {:answer/id #uuid "2cfbfee2-c8fd-5afb-8b32-9dfb5558271c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379196} {:answer/id #uuid "4b379667-5ea1-5281-ac13-348be95c320d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379197} {:answer/id #uuid "2522f8e4-d611-5206-8484-84a6b3f3a51c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379198} {:answer/id #uuid "1daca2a3-6753-580f-a206-189556f21f9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b379667-5ea1-5281-ac13-348be95c320d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379197} :answer-field/id #uuid "60830f8e-0c88-54f4-8f62-c2a959b1a9bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2495c295-7729-594d-b36b-7f04ca3acef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-74223" :question/problem "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2}+{x}_{3}{m}_{3},$ and ${m}_{1}$, ${m}_{2}$, and ${m}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $M.$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -13 & 16\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 2 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=10 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2}+2(-1) & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}-2 & =10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2} & =12 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+(-4)-5(-1) & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+1 & =2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} & =1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1},$ ${m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-4)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}+(-1)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -13\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4)\\cdot (-1)=2.$"}]}
